      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-08-28T13:17:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'll weigh in now - sorry for not doing so earlier!</p><p>Skipping your turn would skip your end phase, certainly. If that were the intent of Prayer of Desperation, it would say \"Skip the rest of your turn.\"</p><p>However, this is a case of \"Proceed directly to end of turn. Do not pass Go. Do not collect 200 Sentinels Points.\" So you would still do any end of turn actions (as few as they may be for Fanatic).</p><p>Does that makes sense?</p>",
